# The death, menu and train scenario (sampcov.pwn commands, one per line; `sleep|S` waits, `shot|NAME` takes a
# screenshot, `key|NAME` presses a key on the DLL client's display): a death by the server's `kill` and the respawn,
# a death in a burning car and the respawn, the forced class selection after a death (RPC 74), a menu with a row
# selected and one left, then the gamemode's static train streamed in. Run after the spawn by samp-rs-ab.sh (CMDS=...)
# on the DLL client and by mod-join.sh (CMDS=...) on the samp mod; mod-join.sh presses the menu's keys on its own
# schedule (MENU_KEYS), as the native game takes keys by iteration only.
